06:29:16,194 --> 06:29:20,255
query menu, execute current statement, right? So,

4316
06:29:20,255 --> 06:29:25,532
Let's execute the first line and then start a transaction and then update the

4317
06:29:25,532 --> 06:29:31,289
points. But we're not going to commit. Now we go to our second session, let me close

4318
06:29:31,289 --> 06:29:36,908
the navigator panel. Alright, here's the second session. In this session we should

4319
06:29:36,908 --> 06:29:42,391
also use our SQL store database, start a transaction, and then try to update the

4320
06:29:42,391 --> 06:29:47,873
customer. Now look at this spinner here. This update is running. Because when we

4321
06:29:47,873 --> 06:29:49,655
executed the first update,

4322
06:29:49,655 --> 06:29:54,653
MySQL put a lock on the customer row that we updated. So if another transaction

4323
06:29:54,653 --> 06:29:59,399
