false is represented as a zero. So we could rewrite this code like this.

4825
07:11:22,416 --> 07:11:28,145
In my opinion, true and false keywords are more descriptive, but I leave it up to

4826
07:11:28,145 --> 07:11:34,015
you to choose the style that you like. What you need to understand is that true and

4827
07:11:34,015 --> 07:11:39,955
false are synonyms for 1 and 0. There are times that you want to restrict the values

4828
07:11:39,955 --> 07:11:45,543
for a column to a limited list of strings. For example, you might have a column

4829
07:11:45,543 --> 07:11:51,483
called size, and in this column, we only want to allow the values small, medium, and

4830
07:11:51,483 --> 07:11:55,656
large. This is where we use the enum type. Let me show you.

4831
07:11:55,656 --> 07:12:01,639
Here in our SQL store database, I'm going to open the products table in the design

