07:12:57,483 --> 07:13:02,629
look at the size of the first product. It's small. So this is how enums work. Now,

4843
07:13:02,629 --> 07:13:07,838
while this may look appealing to you, in my opinion enums are generally bad and you

4844
07:13:07,838 --> 07:13:12,984
should avoid them. The first reason is that changing the members of an enum can be

4845
07:13:12,984 --> 07:13:13,612
expensive.

4846
07:13:13,612 --> 07:13:18,481
For example, let's say tomorrow we decide to come back to our products table and add

4847
07:13:18,481 --> 07:13:23,234
a new member here, or maybe rename one of these members. MySQL is going to rebuild

4848
07:13:23,234 --> 07:13:28,045
this entire table, and this can be expensive if we have millions of records in this

4849
07:13:28,045 --> 07:13:32,913
table. Also with this approach, we can add additional attributes to each member. For

4850
07:13:32,913 --> 07:13:37,782
example, what if we want to include the actual measurements for each size? We can do

4851
07:13:37,782 --> 07:13:38,072
that.

4852
07:13:38,072 --> 07:13:42,413
Also, if you want to get the list of all possible sizes and display them in a drop

4853
07:13:42,413 --> 07:13:46,700
down list in our application, you have to do a bit more work. It's not that easy.

4854
07:13:46,700 --> 07:13:50,935
Plus, these enums are not reusable. So if you have another table and you want to

4855
07:13:50,935 --> 07:13:55,170
