4856
07:13:55,170 --> 07:13:59,458
members. And that duplication means if we decide to make a change in one of these

4857
07:13:59,458 --> 07:14:03,745
members, we'll have to apply that change in multiple places. So these are some of

4858
07:14:03,745 --> 07:14:07,292
the reasons that I believe enums are bad and you should avoid them.

4859
07:14:07,292 --> 07:14:12,372
A better approach is to have a separate table called sizes. In this table we can

4860
07:14:12,372 --> 07:14:17,643
store all the sizes and any additional attributes they have like their measurement.

4861
07:14:17,643 --> 07:14:22,914
We can reuse this table in multiple places and if you want to get all the sizes, we

4862
07:14:22,914 --> 07:14:28,184
write a single select statement, that's really easy. We refer to this kind of table

4863
07:14:28,184 --> 07:14:33,518
as a lookup table. In our SQL invoicing database, this payment methods table is also

4864
07:14:33,518 --> 07:14:34,852
another lookup table.

4865
07:14:34,852 --> 07:14:39,958
Quite often we use these tables to feed our drop down lists. So, back to enums, just

4866
07:14:39,958 --> 07:14:44,943
because MySQL supports them, doesn't mean you should use them. I only explain them

4867
07:14:44,943 --> 07:14:49,624
here so you are aware of them and know why they are bad. We also have another

4868
07:14:49,624 --> 07:14:54,730
similar type called a set, but a set can store multiple values. So similar to enums,

4869
